title: "07d  Payment and settlement: how money moves from the Treasury Single Account to the payee (Modified Disbursement System)"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: the agency holds no cash for its regular budget. Through which accounts does the money pass when the agency pays, and at which moment does cash leave the Treasury?
  %% IDEA: under the Modified Disbursement System (MDS) the servicing bank pays first, from an account that the Treasury keeps funded. The NCA is only a limit recorded at the bank. Cash leaves the Treasury Single Account when BTr replenishes the bank for payments already made.
  %% SOURCES: NCA credited to MDS sub-accounts at LBP, DBP and PVB, lapsing at the end of the quarter [NBC599]. LDDAP-ADA, SLIIE, same-day copy to BTr for replenishment of the MDS seed fund, creditors' bank accounts [CL2013-16A]. Daily replenishment of servicing banks [PRIMER]. eMDS functions and the 24 to 48 hours for credit, Advice of Checks Issued and Cancelled [eMDS]. Treasury Single Account as a unified structure of government bank accounts [BTR-SITE]. Daily bank reconciliation in BTMS, payments by PESONet and InstaPay [BTMS-SITE][CL2025-8].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: step 6 (payee in another bank), steps 8 and 9 (instruction and entries at BSP), step 10 (bank report of items not credited), step 11 (reconciliation in agencies without BTMS).
  participant DBM as DBM
  participant AGY as Agency<br/>(accounting and cash units)
  participant GSB as Servicing bank<br/>(LBP, DBP or PVB)
  participant PB as Payee's<br/>bank account
  participant BTR as BTr
  participant BSP as BSP (Treasury<br/>Single Account)

  DBM->>GSB: NCA: limit for the MDS sub-account of the agency
  AGY->>GSB: LDDAP-ADA with summary list (SLIIE),<br/>on paper or through eMDS
  GSB->>GSB: Check signatories and NCA balance<br/>#nbsp;
  GSB->>GSB: Debit the MDS sub-account (the NCA balance decreases)<br/>#nbsp;
  alt Payee has an account in the same bank
    GSB->>PB: Credit the account, within 24 to 48 hours
  else Payee has an account in another bank
    GSB->>PB: Transfer through an interbank payment system
  end
  GSB->>BTR: Copy of the SLIIE on the same day,<br/>and the report of payments made
  BTR->>BSP: Instruction to replenish the servicing bank
  BSP->>GSB: Debit the Treasury account, credit the account of the bank at BSP
  GSB-->>AGY: Items credited, and items not credited
  AGY->>AGY: Invalidate items not credited. Reconcile the books<br/>with the bank report of the MDS sub-account<br/>#nbsp;

  Note over DBM,BSP: PAYMENT BY CHECK (exception): the agency issues an MDS check and sends the bank an<br/>Advice of Checks Issued and Cancelled. The bank pays only checks listed in the advice.
  Note over DBM,BSP: END OF QUARTER: the unused balance of a regular NCA lapses.<br/>IN AGENCIES THAT USE BTMS: payments are made by electronic transfer (PESONet, InstaPay) or check,<br/>and the system reconciles with electronic bank statements each day.
